<div class="article">
  <h3>Notes from the World Premiere</h3>
  <p>Executive produced by Ed Begley Jr., this timely documentary from filmmaker Rick Cutter investigates what happens when the grid that powers everything starts to fail and AI data centers put additional strain on power grids worldwide.</p>

  <p>Using California's devastating wildfires as a gateway to a larger global story, Cutter speaks with leading energy experts, innovators, and policymakers about the urgent challenge of modernizing the infrastructure that powers our lives.</p>

  <h3>What I wrote down in the theater</h3>
  <p>Forest fires. The grid + weather creating fires. Paradise, CA.</p>

  <p>Why are we so hooked to the grid? Is there a better way?</p>

  <p>The grid started as a small project, but no one really knows how or when it exactly began.</p>

  <blockquote>Rethink, Reduce, Reuse, Recycle, Repair. We need a plan for fire prevention, not just fire response.</blockquote>

  <p>Is time running out and are we losing our home?</p>

  <h3>What stuck with me</h3>
  <p>What stuck with me is how the film doesn't stay in the alarm. It frames the fix as a moon-shot — the same Apollo-era thinking that once put a man on the moon — a common sense pitch for a plan to fix it.</p>

  <p>I couldn't be happier to help bring awareness to this film.</p>

  <p><em>— Panamera Media Co, Live from the 34th Hamptons International Film Festival, Air, Land & Sea Program</em></p>
</div>

